  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="faq-h" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap faqwrap">
      <div><h2 class="h-lg" id="faq-h">Good to know</h2></div>
      <div class="stg faq">
        <details><summary>Are workshops running yet?</summary><div class="ans">Not yet. Own Two Feet is a student venture that’s still in development, so no workshops are running or booking. Join the interest list and we’ll email you when we launch.</div></details>
        <details><summary>Who are the workshops for?</summary><div class="ans">Boys and young men in elementary and middle school. Activities are matched to their age. Topics for older students, like car basics, come later.</div></details>
        <details><summary>Couldn’t students just watch a video?</summary><div class="ans">Videos can show the steps. In a workshop, a real person explains why, fixes mistakes right away, and talks about when to stop.</div></details>
        <details><summary>How do you keep sessions safe?</summary><div class="ans">Everything is supervised and right for their age. Students never work on electrical, gas or other dangerous repairs, and every topic covers when to get an adult or a pro.</div></details>
        <details><summary>What will it cost?</summary><div class="ans">We plan to charge $200 for a 50-minute workshop and $300 for a 90-minute one, per session, for up to 30 students. We bring the supplies. Or run our activities yourself with a monthly online plan: $9.99 a month for a teacher or volunteer who shows proof, or $19.99 a month for a team of three. These are planned prices, and nothing is booking yet.</div></details>
        <details><summary>Will there be manuals?</summary><div class="ans">Yes. We’re writing a free manual for each topic that teachers, parents and students can use at home or in class. Seven are ready to read and print. Vehicle basics is on the way.<a href="manuals/">See the manuals</a>. The five activities on this site are free to try now.</div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

